<details class="disclosure history-help">
  <summary>How to read dates and sources</summary>
  <p><strong>Recorded on</strong> is when the registry detected a value in the official API, not necessarily when the publisher changed it.</p>
  <p><strong>Read from the printed card</strong> means a maintainer transcribed an earlier face that the API never served. Its range starts at the first release carrying those values. An initial API record stands for the period before recording began.</p>
  <p>The ranges are registry history boundaries. They do not establish an official effective date. <a href="/docs/history">Read the history documentation</a>.</p>
</details>
